      "response": "Do not chase the frightened cat or reach under the car. Ask the driver not to move it and keep yourself out of traffic. Call a veterinarian or trained animal handler for help with safe capture. Only if she tolerates handling and you can do it safely, support her body with a towel and place her gently in a secure, ventilated carrier. Keep her face clear and avoid pressure on injuries. A towel does not prevent bites or scratches; stop if she struggles and do not force a capture.\n\nThese institutions are listed in the sources, but clinical treatment access remains unconfirmed:\n\n- AMTM Dana Pani Hospital — CTS 166/167, Ashram, Madh-Marve Road Malad West, Mumbai 400061 — institution listed; clinical treatment access is unconfirmed.\n\nA treatment listing alone does not establish rescue pickup or current availability. Call before travelling to confirm treatment and admission for this animal and the correct emergency location.",
